IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `wills-making`

-- Wills Act 1970 (WA) -- the Q&A layer: the questions people ask, with the seat and the situation as parameters, over the
-- baseline's rules in wills-making.l4.
--
-- PURPOSE. One module whose exported questions serve every seat from one deployment. Every exported question takes
-- `my role` first ("Which of these describes you"). A question about another role answers `does not arise for you`
-- without reading any other input, so the site's form never asks those inputs and drops the question.
--
-- ROLES (type `Role`):
--   * `I am making a will, or have made one` -- the baseline's seat as the will-maker (ss 6-16, 20, 32, 40);
--   * `I am named in the will of someone who has died, or am their family` -- the baseline's seat as the beneficiary
--     (the deleted s 13, ss 7, 8, 26, 27, 32, 33), and the family member who asks what the will gives them;
--   * `I have been asked to witness a will, or have witnessed one` -- new: the witness, on whom s 8(c), (d) and s 11 bear
--     directly, and who asks whether witnessing costs them a gift (the deleted s 13).
-- The Supreme Court and the Principal Registrar are never a seat; what they may do appears as what it means for the
-- person asking.
--
-- SITUATIONS (graffiti design D8). Within a role, a question that arises only in a situation takes that situation's
-- fact straight after `my role`, and answers `does not arise for you` when it does not hold, without reading anything
-- else. The questions of one situation share one input, the same name, type and @desc:
--   * will-maker: `I have married since making the will` (s 14(1)); `my will was made in contemplation of a marriage`
--     (s 14(2)); `something has happened to my marriage since I made the will` (s 14A, two questions); `my will has been
--     revoked` (s 16(1));
--   * beneficiary or family: none. The role is someone named in the will of a person who has died, or their family, so
--     the death holds by the role's own terms and its questions (ss 13, 26, 27, 32, 33 and validity at death) arise for
--     every such person (fixed 6 November 2026; it was a situation input of five questions).
-- A question that arises in every situation of its role takes no situation input: the will-maker's capacity, formality,
-- s 20, alteration, revocation and statutory-will questions, the deleted s 13 for each role, and the witness's three.
--
-- No helper here reads a situation enumeration: every situation is a BOOLEAN, read by IF, so an ASSUMEd value read in the
-- cases fails. The helpers that read the one choice input, `another route to a valid will`, list every value with no
-- OTHERWISE (graffiti finding 31).
--
-- The rules are the baseline's; this module builds its records from plain answers and calls its functions, restating
-- none. A record field or input that no rule reads on the path a question takes gets a fixed value, with a comment. No
-- exported question takes a DEONTIC or EVENT input. BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md, "Q&A layer
-- (seat and situations as parameters)".

§ `Wills Act 1970 (WA) -- the questions people ask`

§§ `Who is asking, and the shape of the answers`

DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `I am making a will, or have made one`
    `I am named in the will of someone who has died, or am their family`
    `I have been asked to witness a will, or have witnessed one`

DECLARE `Yes or no` IS ONE OF
    yes
    no
    `does not arise for you`

DECLARE `What happens to the witness's gift` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `nothing in this Act takes the gift away from the witness`
    `not covered: the deleted section 13 may still apply, and its text is not in the deposit`

DECLARE `Whether the document is the will` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `it is the will, because the Supreme Court is satisfied the will-maker intended it to be (s 32)`
    `not while the will-maker is living: s 32 applies only to the document of a deceased person`
    `not a will: the Supreme Court is not satisfied the will-maker intended it to be`
    `not a will: s 33 confines s 32 to deaths on or after 9 February 2008`

DECLARE `What becomes of a gift` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the gift takes effect as it is written`
    `as the will itself provides for this case`
    `it passes to the beneficiary's children who survive the will-maker, in equal shares`
    `the share accrues to the other shares`
    `the gift falls into the residue`
    `it is not disposed of by the will (intestacy, under the Administration Act 1903)`

§§ `Building the baseline's inputs`

GIVEN `it holds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`yes if` `it holds` MEANS
    IF `it holds` THEN yes ELSE no

GIVEN `in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `signed by the will-maker` IS A BOOLEAN
      `signed for the will-maker` IS A BOOLEAN
      `signature shows intent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `witnesses together` IS A NUMBER
      `witnesses unable to see` IS A NUMBER
      `witnesses signed in presence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a witness takes a gift` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `My will's signing`
`the signing from` `in writing` `signed by the will-maker` `signed for the will-maker` `signature shows intent` `witnesses together` `witnesses unable to see` `witnesses signed in presence` `a witness takes a gift` MEANS
    `My will's signing` WITH
        `it is in writing` IS `in writing`
        `I signed it` IS `signed by the will-maker`
        `someone signed it for me, in my presence and at my direction` IS `signed for the will-maker`
        `the signature shows I meant it to give effect to the will` IS `signature shows intent`
        `witnesses present together when I signed or acknowledged` IS `witnesses together`
        `of them, unable to see and attest that I signed` IS `witnesses unable to see`
        `the witnesses signed in my presence` IS `witnesses signed in presence`
        `a witness, or a witness's spouse, takes a gift under it` IS `a witness takes a gift`

GIVEN `other law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `law of the land` IS A BOOLEAN
      `international` IS A BOOLEAN
      `statutory` IS A BOOLEAN
      `privileged` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Another route`
`the route from` `other law` `law of the land` `international` `statutory` `privileged` MEANS
    `Another route` WITH
        `it conforms to the law of where it was signed, or of my domicile, habitual residence or nationality` IS `other law`
        `it conforms to the law of where the land or building is` IS `law of the land`
        `it is an international will under Annex Articles 2 to 5` IS `international`
        `it is a statutory will signed by the Principal Registrar and sealed` IS `statutory`
        `it is a privileged will saved by section 17` IS `privileged`

-- The routes to a valid will other than s 8, as one choice (NOTES, Q&A layer, QA1). The baseline reads s 20(1), s 20(2)(b)
-- with `as to land or a building`, Part XA and Part XI only joined by OR (`Is my will formally valid`), and s 20 only as
-- s 20(1) OR (land AND s 20(2)(b)), so one value that holds gives the baseline the answer it gives every will with that
-- route, and `none of these` the answer it gives every will with none. s 17 (a privileged will) stays its own input,
-- because s 7 reads it too.
DECLARE `Another route to a valid will` IS ONE OF
    `none of these`
    `it conforms to the law of where it was signed, or of the will-maker's domicile, habitual residence or nationality (s 20(1))`
    `as to land or a building, it conforms to the law of where the land or building is (s 20(2)(b))`
    `it is an international will under Annex Articles 2 to 5 (Part XA)`
    `it is a statutory will signed by the Principal Registrar and sealed (Part XI)`

-- Every value is listed, with no OTHERWISE (graffiti finding 31).
GIVEN `the route` IS AN `Another route to a valid will`
      `privileged` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Another route`
`the route for` `the route` `privileged` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the route`
    WHEN `none of these` THEN `the route from` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `privileged`
    WHEN `it conforms to the law of where it was signed, or of the will-maker's domicile, habitual residence or nationality (s 20(1))` THEN `the route from` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `privileged`
    WHEN `as to land or a building, it conforms to the law of where the land or building is (s 20(2)(b))` THEN `the route from` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `privileged`
    WHEN `it is an international will under Annex Articles 2 to 5 (Part XA)` THEN `the route from` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `privileged`
    WHEN `it is a statutory will signed by the Principal Registrar and sealed (Part XI)` THEN `the route from` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE `privileged`

GIVEN `the route` IS AN `Another route to a valid will`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`it is as to land` `the route` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the route`
    WHEN `none of these` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `it conforms to the law of where it was signed, or of the will-maker's domicile, habitual residence or nationality (s 20(1))` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `as to land or a building, it conforms to the law of where the land or building is (s 20(2)(b))` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `it is an international will under Annex Articles 2 to 5 (Part XA)` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `it is a statutory will signed by the Principal Registrar and sealed (Part XI)` THEN FALSE

GIVEN `survived` IS A BOOLEAN
      `issue` IS A BOOLEAN
      `not determinable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `left a child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `joint tenant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `fractional share` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the residue itself` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a residuary gift` IS A BOOLEAN
      `contrary intention` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The gift`
`the gift from` `survived` `issue` `not determinable` `left a child` `joint tenant` `fractional share` `the residue itself` `a residuary gift` `contrary intention` MEANS
    `The gift` WITH
        `the beneficiary survived the will-maker` IS `survived`
        `the beneficiary is a child or other issue of the will-maker` IS `issue`
        `the gift was not to end at or before the beneficiary's death` IS `not determinable`
        `the beneficiary left a child who survived the will-maker` IS `left a child`
        `given to the beneficiary as a joint tenant` IS `joint tenant`
        `a fractional share of the whole or residue, and another share takes effect` IS `fractional share`
        `itself the residue or the whole estate` IS `the residue itself`
        `the will has a residuary gift` IS `a residuary gift`
        `the will shows a contrary intention` IS `contrary intention`

GIVEN `the answer` IS A `What happens to a witness's gift`
GIVETH A `What happens to the witness's gift`
`the witness answer` `the answer` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer`
    WHEN `nothing in this Act takes the gift away` THEN `nothing in this Act takes the gift away from the witness`
    WHEN `the deleted section 13 may still apply, and its text is not in the deposit: not covered by this encoding` THEN `not covered: the deleted section 13 may still apply, and its text is not in the deposit`

GIVEN `the answer` IS A `What becomes of my informal document`
GIVETH A `Whether the document is the will`
`the informal document answer` `the answer` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer`
    WHEN `it is my will, because the Supreme Court is satisfied I intended it to be (s 32)` THEN `it is the will, because the Supreme Court is satisfied the will-maker intended it to be (s 32)`
    WHEN `not while I am living: s 32 applies only to the document of a deceased person` THEN `not while the will-maker is living: s 32 applies only to the document of a deceased person`
    WHEN `not a will: the Supreme Court is not satisfied I intended it to be` THEN `not a will: the Supreme Court is not satisfied the will-maker intended it to be`
    WHEN `not a will: s 33 confines s 32 to deaths on or after 9 February 2008` THEN `not a will: s 33 confines s 32 to deaths on or after 9 February 2008`

GIVEN `the answer` IS A `What becomes of the gift`
GIVETH A `What becomes of a gift`
`the gift answer` `the answer` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer`
    WHEN `the gift takes effect` THEN `the gift takes effect as it is written`
    WHEN `as the will itself provides` THEN `as the will itself provides for this case`
    WHEN `it passes to the beneficiary's children who survive, in equal shares` THEN `it passes to the beneficiary's children who survive the will-maker, in equal shares`
    WHEN `the share accrues to the other shares` THEN `the share accrues to the other shares`
    WHEN `the gift falls into the residue` THEN `the gift falls into the residue`
    WHEN `it is not disposed of by the will` THEN `it is not disposed of by the will (intestacy, under the Administration Act 1903)`

-- A will-maker who asks is living. Where a question turns on the date of death, a living will-maker's death is after
-- 9 February 2008 by the role's own terms, so that date stands in for it; and where it turns on whether the will-maker
-- has died, FALSE does. On the s 32 path a living will-maker's date of death and the Court's satisfaction are not read.
`a death after the 2008 amendments` MEANS `the day the Wills Amendment Act 2007 commenced`

§§ `For the person making a will`

§§§ `ss 6, 7 -- what my will may do, and am I old enough`

@export May my will make this provision: a gift of what I own at death (on trust or not), an appointment under a power, a guardian for my infant child (Wills Act 1970 (WA) s 6)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the provision` IS A Provision @desc What you want your will to do
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May my will provide for this` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am making a will, or have made one` THEN `yes if` (`May my will make this provision` `the provision`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Was I old enough, 18, to make a valid will on the day I made it (Wills Act 1970 (WA) s 7; s 17 saves a privileged will)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the will-maker's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc The will-maker's date of birth (yours, if the will is yours)
      `the date the will was made` IS A DATE @desc The date the will was signed (or made)
      `it is a privileged will saved by section 17` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the will was made under the former s 18 (soldiers', sailors' and airmen's wills) before its repeal, and is saved by s 17
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Was I old enough to make my will` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am making a will, or have made one` THEN `yes if` (`Am I old enough to make a valid will` `the will-maker's date of birth` `the date the will was made` `it is a privileged will saved by section 17`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 8, 11, 13 (deleted) -- signing and witnessing my will`

@export May this person act as a witness to my will: anyone who can see and attest that I signed, a beneficiary included (Wills Act 1970 (WA) s 11)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the witness is able to see and attest the signing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the witness is able to see, and attest, that the will-maker signed
      `the witness, or the witness's spouse, takes a gift under the will` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the witness, or the witness's spouse, is a beneficiary under the will
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May this person be a witness to my will` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am making a will, or have made one` THEN `yes if` (`May this person witness my will` `the witness is able to see and attest the signing` `the witness, or the witness's spouse, takes a gift under the will`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is my will signed and witnessed as the Act requires: in writing, signed by me or for me, before 2 witnesses present together who each can see, and who sign in my presence (Wills Act 1970 (WA) ss 8, 11)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `it is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the will is in writing
      `the will-maker signed it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the will-maker signed it
      `someone signed it for the will-maker, in their presence and at their direction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether someone else signed it in the will-maker's name, in the will-maker's presence and by their direction
      `the signature shows the will-maker meant it to give effect to the will` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the signature is placed so that it is apparent on the face of the will that the will-maker meant it to give effect to the will
      `witnesses present together at the signing` IS A NUMBER @desc How many witnesses were present together when the will-maker signed or acknowledged the signature
      `of them, unable to see and attest the signing` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of those witnesses were unable to see and attest that the will-maker signed
      `the witnesses signed in the will-maker's presence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the witnesses attested and signed the will in the will-maker's presence
      `a witness, or a witness's spouse, takes a gift under it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a witness, or a witness's spouse, takes a gift under the will (it changes nothing under s 8)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is my will properly signed and witnessed` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am making a will, or have made one` THEN `yes if` (`Is my will signed and witnessed as section 8 requires` (`the signing from` `it is in writing` `the will-maker signed it` `someone signed it for the will-maker, in their presence and at their direction` `the signature shows the will-maker meant it to give effect to the will` `witnesses present together at the signing` `of them, unable to see and attest the signing` `the witnesses signed in the will-maker's presence` `a witness, or a witness's spouse, takes a gift under it`))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- s 13 (deleted): the will-maker asking is living, so dies after 1 July 2003; the baseline is asked with a date after it.
@export If a witness to my will, or the witness's spouse, takes a gift under it, does the witness lose the gift (Wills Act 1970 (WA), s 13 deleted from 1 July 2003)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `What happens to the witness's gift`
`Does my witness lose the gift` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am making a will, or have made one` THEN `the witness answer` (`Does a witness lose a gift under my will` `a death after the 2008 amendments`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 17, 20, 32, Parts XA, X, XI -- the other routes to a valid will`

@export Is my will taken to be properly executed under another place's law: where signed, my domicile, residence or nationality, or for land, where it is (Wills Act 1970 (WA) s 20(1), (2)(b))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `another route to a valid will` IS AN `Another route to a valid will` @desc Whether the will is valid in form by a route other than s 8: it conforms to the law of where it was signed, or of the will-maker's domicile, habitual residence or nationality (s 20(1)); as to land or a building it disposes of, it conforms to the law of where that is (s 20(2)(b)); it is an international will (Part XA); it is a statutory will (Part XI); or none of these
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is my will properly executed under another place's law` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am making a will, or have made one` THEN `yes if` (`Is my will properly executed under section 20` (`the route for` `another route to a valid will` FALSE) (`it is as to land` `another route to a valid will`))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- For the will-maker, who is living, the answer is s 32's own: not while living. It settles on the role.
@export Can a document I did not sign and have witnessed, such as a video or a text message, take effect as my will (Wills Act 1970 (WA) ss 32, 33)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `Whether the document is the will`
`Can my unwitnessed document be my will` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am making a will, or have made one` THEN `the informal document answer` (`Can my informal document be my will` FALSE `a death after the 2008 amendments` FALSE)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- The will-maker is living, so the s 32 route is not open: FALSE for the death and the Court, the date standing in.
@export Is my will valid as to form, by s 8 or by another route: another place's law, an international will, a statutory will, or a privileged will (Wills Act 1970 (WA) ss 8, 17, 20, Parts XA, XI; Part X only after death)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `it is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the will is in writing
      `the will-maker signed it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the will-maker signed it
      `someone signed it for the will-maker, in their presence and at their direction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether someone else signed it in the will-maker's name, in the will-maker's presence and by their direction
      `the signature shows the will-maker meant it to give effect to the will` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the signature is placed so that it is apparent on the face of the will that the will-maker meant it to give effect to the will
      `witnesses present together at the signing` IS A NUMBER @desc How many witnesses were present together when the will-maker signed or acknowledged the signature
      `of them, unable to see and attest the signing` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of those witnesses were unable to see and attest that the will-maker signed
      `the witnesses signed in the will-maker's presence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the witnesses attested and signed the will in the will-maker's presence
      `another route to a valid will` IS AN `Another route to a valid will` @desc Whether the will is valid in form by a route other than s 8: it conforms to the law of where it was signed, or of the will-maker's domicile, habitual residence or nationality (s 20(1)); as to land or a building it disposes of, it conforms to the law of where that is (s 20(2)(b)); it is an international will (Part XA); it is a statutory will (Part XI); or none of these
      `it is a privileged will saved by section 17` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the will was made under the former s 18 (soldiers', sailors' and airmen's wills) before its repeal, and is saved by s 17
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is my will valid in form` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am making a will, or have made one` THEN `yes if` (`Is my will formally valid` (`the signing from` `it is in writing` `the will-maker signed it` `someone signed it for the will-maker, in their presence and at their direction` `the signature shows the will-maker meant it to give effect to the will` `witnesses present together at the signing` `of them, unable to see and attest the signing` `the witnesses signed in the will-maker's presence` FALSE) (`the route for` `another route to a valid will` `it is a privileged will saved by section 17`) (`it is as to land` `another route to a valid will`) FALSE `a death after the 2008 amendments` FALSE)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is my will valid, as to my age when I made it and its form (Wills Act 1970 (WA) ss 7, 8, 17, 20, Parts XA, XI)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the will-maker's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc The will-maker's date of birth (yours, if the will is yours)
      `the date the will was made` IS A DATE @desc The date the will was signed (or made)
      `it is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the will is in writing
      `the will-maker signed it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the will-maker signed it
      `someone signed it for the will-maker, in their presence and at their direction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether someone else signed it in the will-maker's name, in the will-maker's presence and by their direction
      `the signature shows the will-maker meant it to give effect to the will` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the signature is placed so that it is apparent on the face of the will that the will-maker meant it to give effect to the will
      `witnesses present together at the signing` IS A NUMBER @desc How many witnesses were present together when the will-maker signed or acknowledged the signature
      `of them, unable to see and attest the signing` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of those witnesses were unable to see and attest that the will-maker signed
      `the witnesses signed in the will-maker's presence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the witnesses attested and signed the will in the will-maker's presence
      `another route to a valid will` IS AN `Another route to a valid will` @desc Whether the will is valid in form by a route other than s 8: it conforms to the law of where it was signed, or of the will-maker's domicile, habitual residence or nationality (s 20(1)); as to land or a building it disposes of, it conforms to the law of where that is (s 20(2)(b)); it is an international will (Part XA); it is a statutory will (Part XI); or none of these
      `it is a privileged will saved by section 17` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the will was made under the former s 18 (soldiers', sailors' and airmen's wills) before its repeal, and is saved by s 17
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is the will I made valid` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am making a will, or have made one` THEN `yes if` (`Is my will valid` `the will-maker's date of birth` `the date the will was made` (`the signing from` `it is in writing` `the will-maker signed it` `someone signed it for the will-maker, in their presence and at their direction` `the signature shows the will-maker meant it to give effect to the will` `witnesses present together at the signing` `of them, unable to see and attest the signing` `the witnesses signed in the will-maker's presence` FALSE) (`the route for` `another route to a valid will` `it is a privileged will saved by section 17`) (`it is as to land` `another route to a valid will`) FALSE `a death after the 2008 amendments` FALSE)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 10 -- changing my will after signing it`

@export Is my change to my will after signing it effective: only if signed and witnessed as a will, or if it makes the old words no longer apparent, or if the Supreme Court accepts it (Wills Act 1970 (WA) s 10)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I signed and had the change witnessed as for a will` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the alteration itself was executed as a will must be
      `I made it, or directed it, and the original words can no longer be read even with a magnifying lens` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the alteration obliterates the words so they are no longer apparent
      `the Supreme Court accepts it under Part X` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Supreme Court is satisfied, after your death, that you intended the alteration
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does my change to the will count` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am making a will, or have made one` THEN `yes if` (`Is my alteration effective` `I signed and had the change witnessed as for a will` `I made it, or directed it, and the original words can no longer be read even with a magnifying lens` `the Supreme Court accepts it under Part X`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 14, 14A -- marriage, and the end of a marriage`

-- s 14(1): the marriage is the situation, and the baseline's first input; TRUE by the situation's own terms.
@export I have married since making my will: does the marriage revoke it, unless it was made in contemplation of the marriage (Wills Act 1970 (WA) s 14(1), (3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have married since making the will` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have married since you made the will
      `the will says it is made in contemplation of that marriage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the will is expressed to be made in contemplation of the marriage
      `other evidence shows it was made in contemplation of that marriage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there is other evidence that the will was made in contemplation of the marriage
      `the will only appoints property that would not go to my personal representatives` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the will is an appointment under a power whose property would not, in default, pass to your personal representatives
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Has my marriage revoked my will` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am making a will, or have made one` THEN
        IF `I have married since making the will`
        THEN `yes if` (`Does my marriage revoke my will` TRUE `the will says it is made in contemplation of that marriage` `other evidence shows it was made in contemplation of that marriage` `the will only appoints property that would not go to my personal representatives`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- s 14(2): the will made in contemplation of a marriage is the situation, and the baseline's first input.
@export My will was made in contemplation of a marriage: is it void because the marriage did not take place (Wills Act 1970 (WA) s 14(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my will was made in contemplation of a marriage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your will was made in contemplation of a particular marriage (it says so, or other evidence shows it)
      `the marriage was solemnised` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that marriage took place
      `the will provides to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the will says it stands even if the marriage does not happen
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is my will void for the marriage that did not happen` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am making a will, or have made one` THEN
        IF `my will was made in contemplation of a marriage`
        THEN `yes if` (`Is my will void because the marriage did not happen` TRUE `the marriage was solemnised` `the will provides to the contrary`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Has my marriage ended, for the Act: a divorce order taking effect, a decree of nullity, or a foreign dissolution recognised in Australia, but not separation or my spouse's death (Wills Act 1970 (WA) s 14A(3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `something has happened to my marriage since I made the will` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, since you made the will, your marriage has been ended by divorce, nullity or a foreign dissolution, you have separated, or your spouse has died
      `what happened to my marriage` IS A `What happened to my marriage` @desc What happened to your marriage
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Has my marriage ended under the Act` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am making a will, or have made one` THEN
        IF `something has happened to my marriage since I made the will`
        THEN `yes if` (`Has my marriage ended for section 14A` `what happened to my marriage`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Does the end of my marriage revoke my will, unless the will or other evidence shows I meant it to stand (Wills Act 1970 (WA) s 14A; only for a marriage ending on or after 9 February 2008)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `something has happened to my marriage since I made the will` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, since you made the will, your marriage has been ended by divorce, nullity or a foreign dissolution, you have separated, or your spouse has died
      `what happened to my marriage` IS A `What happened to my marriage` @desc What happened to your marriage
      `the date it happened` IS A DATE @desc The date the divorce order took effect (or the other event happened)
      `the will shows a contrary intention to the ending` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the will says it is to stand despite the marriage ending
      `other evidence shows that intention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether other evidence shows you meant the will to stand despite the marriage ending
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Has the end of my marriage revoked my will` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am making a will, or have made one` THEN
        IF `something has happened to my marriage since I made the will`
        THEN `yes if` (`Does the end of my marriage revoke my will` `what happened to my marriage` `the date it happened` `the will shows a contrary intention to the ending` `other evidence shows that intention`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 15, 16 -- revoking my will, and bringing it back`

@export Does what I did revoke my will: a later will, a witnessed writing, or destroying it meaning to revoke it, by me or in my presence at my direction (Wills Act 1970 (WA) s 15)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `what I did` IS A `What I did` @desc What you did to revoke the will
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Have I revoked my will` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am making a will, or have made one` THEN `yes if` (`Does what I did revoke my will` `what I did`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export My will has been revoked: can I bring it back, by re-executing it or by a later will showing I mean to revive it (Wills Act 1970 (WA) s 16(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my will has been revoked` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your will (or part of it) has been revoked
      `I re-executed the revoked will` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you signed and had the old will witnessed again
      `I executed a later will showing an intention to revive it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a later will (or a document accepted under Part X) shows you meant to revive the old will
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Have I revived my revoked will` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am making a will, or have made one` THEN
        IF `my will has been revoked`
        THEN `yes if` (`Is my revoked will revived` `I re-executed the revoked will` `I executed a later will showing an intention to revive it`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 40, 42 -- a will made for me if I lose capacity`

@export If I lose capacity, may the Supreme Court authorise a will on my behalf: only while I live, am 18 or over and lack capacity, and the Court is satisfied of the s 42(1) matters (Wills Act 1970 (WA) ss 40, 42)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I am living when the order is made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are living when the order is made
      `my age when the order is made` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age, in completed years, when the order is made
      `I lack testamentary capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you lack testamentary capacity
      `the Court is satisfied of section 42(1)(a) to (d)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court is satisfied of each matter in s 42(1)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May the Court make a will for me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am making a will, or have made one` THEN `yes if` (`May the Court authorise a will for me` `I am living when the order is made` `my age when the order is made` `I lack testamentary capacity` `the Court is satisfied of section 42(1)(a) to (d)`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For a beneficiary of a will, or the family of someone who has died`

§§§ `ss 7, 8, 13 (deleted), 32, 33 -- is the will valid`

-- The beneficiary or family asks after the death (the role's own terms), so the date is asked. A witness may ask while
-- the will-maker lives: then the death will come after 1 July 2003, and the date in `a death after the 2008 amendments`
-- stands in for it, as for the will-maker; the date is asked only if the will-maker has died. `the will-maker has died`
-- is an ordinary input here, not a situation: the question arises for the witness either way.
@export I witnessed the will, or my spouse did: do I lose my gift under it (Wills Act 1970 (WA), s 13 deleted from 1 July 2003, for deaths on or after that day)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the will-maker has died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the will-maker has died
      `the date the will-maker died` IS A DATE @desc The date the will-maker died
GIVETH A `What happens to the witness's gift`
`Do I lose my gift as a witness` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am named in the will of someone who has died, or am their family` THEN `the witness answer` (`Does a witness lose a gift under my will` `the date the will-maker died`)
    WHEN `I have been asked to witness a will, or have witnessed one` THEN
        IF `the will-maker has died`
        THEN `the witness answer` (`Does a witness lose a gift under my will` `the date the will-maker died`)
        ELSE `the witness answer` (`Does a witness lose a gift under my will` `a death after the 2008 amendments`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- The death is the baseline's first input: TRUE by the role's own terms.
@export The will-maker has died: can a document they did not sign and have witnessed, such as a video or a text message, take effect as their will (Wills Act 1970 (WA) ss 32, 33: if the Supreme Court is satisfied they intended it, for deaths on or after 9 February 2008)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the date the will-maker died` IS A DATE @desc The date the will-maker died
      `the Supreme Court is satisfied the will-maker intended it as their will` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Supreme Court is (or would be) satisfied that the will-maker intended the document to be their will
GIVETH A `Whether the document is the will`
`Can the deceased's document be their will` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am named in the will of someone who has died, or am their family` THEN `the informal document answer` (`Can my informal document be my will` TRUE `the date the will-maker died` `the Supreme Court is satisfied the will-maker intended it as their will`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export The will-maker has died: was the will valid, as to their age and its form, s 32 included (Wills Act 1970 (WA) ss 7, 8, 17, 20, 32, 33, Parts XA, XI)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the will-maker's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc The will-maker's date of birth (yours, if the will is yours)
      `the date the will was made` IS A DATE @desc The date the will was signed (or made)
      `it is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the will is in writing
      `the will-maker signed it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the will-maker signed it
      `someone signed it for the will-maker, in their presence and at their direction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether someone else signed it in the will-maker's name, in the will-maker's presence and by their direction
      `the signature shows the will-maker meant it to give effect to the will` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the signature is placed so that it is apparent on the face of the will that the will-maker meant it to give effect to the will
      `witnesses present together at the signing` IS A NUMBER @desc How many witnesses were present together when the will-maker signed or acknowledged the signature
      `of them, unable to see and attest the signing` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of those witnesses were unable to see and attest that the will-maker signed
      `the witnesses signed in the will-maker's presence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the witnesses attested and signed the will in the will-maker's presence
      `another route to a valid will` IS AN `Another route to a valid will` @desc Whether the will is valid in form by a route other than s 8: it conforms to the law of where it was signed, or of the will-maker's domicile, habitual residence or nationality (s 20(1)); as to land or a building it disposes of, it conforms to the law of where that is (s 20(2)(b)); it is an international will (Part XA); it is a statutory will (Part XI); or none of these
      `it is a privileged will saved by section 17` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the will was made under the former s 18 (soldiers', sailors' and airmen's wills) before its repeal, and is saved by s 17
      `the date the will-maker died` IS A DATE @desc The date the will-maker died
      `the Supreme Court is satisfied the will-maker intended it as their will` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Supreme Court is (or would be) satisfied that the will-maker intended the document to be their will
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Was the deceased's will valid` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am named in the will of someone who has died, or am their family` THEN `yes if` (`Is my will valid` `the will-maker's date of birth` `the date the will was made` (`the signing from` `it is in writing` `the will-maker signed it` `someone signed it for the will-maker, in their presence and at their direction` `the signature shows the will-maker meant it to give effect to the will` `witnesses present together at the signing` `of them, unable to see and attest the signing` `the witnesses signed in the will-maker's presence` FALSE) (`the route for` `another route to a valid will` `it is a privileged will saved by section 17`) (`it is as to land` `another route to a valid will`) TRUE `the date the will-maker died` `the Supreme Court is satisfied the will-maker intended it as their will`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 26(1)(b), (g), 27 -- what becomes of a gift`

@export The will-maker has died: what becomes of this gift in the will, if the beneficiary died first (Wills Act 1970 (WA) ss 26(1)(b), (g), 27; what the will does not dispose of passes on intestacy)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the beneficiary survived the will-maker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the beneficiary of the gift survived the will-maker
      `the beneficiary is a child or other issue of the will-maker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the beneficiary is a child, grandchild or other descendant of the will-maker
      `the gift was not to end at or before the beneficiary's death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the gift was for an interest not ending at or before the beneficiary's own death (for example, an outright gift, not a life interest)
      `the beneficiary left a child who survived the will-maker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the beneficiary left a child who survived the will-maker
      `given to the beneficiary as a joint tenant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the gift was to the beneficiary as one of two or more joint tenants
      `a fractional share of the whole or residue, and another share takes effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the gift was a fractional share (such as a half) of the whole estate or of the residue, and another share takes effect
      `itself the residue or the whole estate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the gift was itself the residue or the whole estate
      `the will has a residuary gift` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the will has a gift of the residue (what is left)
      `the will shows a contrary intention about this case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the will itself says what is to happen if the beneficiary dies first
GIVETH A `What becomes of a gift`
`What becomes of this gift` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am named in the will of someone who has died, or am their family` THEN `the gift answer` (`What becomes of the gift in my will` (`the gift from` `the beneficiary survived the will-maker` `the beneficiary is a child or other issue of the will-maker` `the gift was not to end at or before the beneficiary's death` `the beneficiary left a child who survived the will-maker` `given to the beneficiary as a joint tenant` `a fractional share of the whole or residue, and another share takes effect` `itself the residue or the whole estate` `the will has a residuary gift` `the will shows a contrary intention about this case`))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- s 27 is asked by the child of the beneficiary who died first: "the beneficiary survived" is FALSE and "left a child"
-- TRUE by the question's own terms (the asker is that child and survived the will-maker).
@export The will-maker has died: my parent, a child or other issue of theirs named in the will, died before them; do I take my parent's gift (Wills Act 1970 (WA) s 27)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the beneficiary is a child or other issue of the will-maker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the beneficiary is a child, grandchild or other descendant of the will-maker
      `the gift was not to end at or before the beneficiary's death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the gift was for an interest not ending at or before the beneficiary's own death (for example, an outright gift, not a life interest)
      `given to the beneficiary as a joint tenant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the gift was to the beneficiary as one of two or more joint tenants
      `the will shows a contrary intention about this case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the will itself says what is to happen if the beneficiary dies first
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Do I take my parent's gift` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am named in the will of someone who has died, or am their family` THEN `yes if` (`Do the beneficiary's children take the gift under section 27` (`the gift from` FALSE `the beneficiary is a child or other issue of the will-maker` `the gift was not to end at or before the beneficiary's death` TRUE `given to the beneficiary as a joint tenant` FALSE FALSE FALSE `the will shows a contrary intention about this case`))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export The will-maker has died and left me out: does the Wills Act give me a share the will does not (Wills Act 1970 (WA); a claim against the estate is the Family Provision Act 1972, intestacy the Administration Act 1903)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I am a child of the will-maker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a child of the person who made the will
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does the Act give me a share the will left out` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am named in the will of someone who has died, or am their family` THEN `yes if` (`Does this Act give me a share the will does not` `I am a child of the will-maker`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For a witness to a will`

§§§ `ss 8(c), (d), 11, 13 (deleted) -- witnessing a will`

@export May I act as a witness to this will: anyone able to see and attest that the will-maker signed may, even one who takes a gift under it (Wills Act 1970 (WA) s 11)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the witness is able to see and attest the signing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the witness is able to see, and attest, that the will-maker signed
      `the witness, or the witness's spouse, takes a gift under the will` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the witness, or the witness's spouse, is a beneficiary under the will
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I witness this will` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I have been asked to witness a will, or have witnessed one` THEN `yes if` (`May this person witness my will` `the witness is able to see and attest the signing` `the witness, or the witness's spouse, takes a gift under the will`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- The witness asks about the witnessing alone, the will being in writing and signed by the will-maker so as to show
-- the intent (s 8(a), (b)): those three are TRUE, and no other signer, by the question's own terms.
@export The will is in writing and the will-maker signed it: is our witnessing enough, 2 witnesses present together who can each see, signing in the will-maker's presence (Wills Act 1970 (WA) s 8(c), (d), s 11; no form of attestation is needed)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `witnesses present together at the signing` IS A NUMBER @desc How many witnesses were present together when the will-maker signed or acknowledged the signature
      `of them, unable to see and attest the signing` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of those witnesses were unable to see and attest that the will-maker signed
      `the witnesses signed in the will-maker's presence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the witnesses attested and signed the will in the will-maker's presence
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is our witnessing of the will enough` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I have been asked to witness a will, or have witnessed one` THEN `yes if` (`Is my will signed and witnessed as section 8 requires` (`the signing from` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE `witnesses present together at the signing` `of them, unable to see and attest the signing` `the witnesses signed in the will-maker's presence` FALSE))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`
